UnitGEOToken::constants
└── when deployed
    └── it sets _GEO_TOKEN_STORAGE_LOCATION to keccak256(abi.encode(uint256(keccak256("geo.storage.GEOToken")) - 1)) & ~bytes32(uint256(0xff))

UnitGEOToken::constructor
└── when called
    └── it disables initializers

UnitGEOToken::initialize
├── when passing valid parameters
│   ├── it sets the token name and symbol
│   ├── it sets the owner
│   ├── it sets the minter
│   ├── it mints initial supply to initial supply recipient
│   └── it emits the MinterSet event
├── when called twice
│   └── it reverts with InvalidInitialization
├── when owner is zero
│   └── it reverts with OwnableInvalidOwner
├── when minter is zero
│   └── it reverts with InvalidAddress
└── when initial supply recipient is zero
    └── it reverts with InvalidAddress

UnitGEOToken::mint
├── when called by minter
│   ├── when amount is greater than zero
│   │   ├── it mints tokens to recipient
│   │   └── it emits Transfer event
│   └── when amount is zero
│       └── it reverts with ZeroAmount
└── when called by non-minter
    └── it reverts with OnlyMinter

UnitGEOToken::burn
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it reverts with ZeroAmount
├── when caller has sufficient balance
│   ├── it burns tokens from caller
│   └── it emits Transfer event
└── when caller has insufficient balance
    └── it reverts with ERC20InsufficientBalance

UnitGEOToken::setMinter
├── when called by owner
│   ├── it sets the new minter address
│   └── it emits the MinterSet event
├── when called by non-owner
│   └── it reverts with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
└── when minter is zero
    └── it reverts with InvalidAddress

UnitGEOToken::typeId
└── when called
    └── it returns the type

UnitGEOToken::version
└── when called
    └── it returns semantic version

UnitGEOToken::nonces
└── when called
    └── it returns the nonce

UnitGEOToken::_authorizeUpgrade
├── when called by owner
│   └── it authorizes the upgrade
└── when called by non-owner
    └── it reverts with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount 